in) (LICENSE)

What was rewritten: the plugin's Python MCP client and its seven tools
(chorepilot_status, chorepilot_chores, chorepilot_who_has, chorepilot_done,
chorepilot_whoami, chorepilot_tools, chorepilot_call) as Common Lisp tools
of one Nodecode cell, on the same JSON-RPC over streamable HTTP to
ChorePilot's own server: initialize, tools/list, tools/call, an
Mcp-Session-Id kept until the server forgets it, and the confirmation and
approval sentences added to a result. The plugin's refusal of plain http to
anything but this machine or a private network became a check at the cell's
start; its skill's household rules became (help :chorepilot); its
registration-time look at the house's tool list, which fills the call
tool's description, is kept, bounded by two seconds and optional
(preload_tools). A /chorepilot command was added for the operator.

What was left out: the Hermes plugin manifest and its environment-variable
wiring (CHOREPILOT_URL, CHOREPILOT_TOKEN, CHOREPILOT_TIMEOUT), replaced by
the cell's config section; the per-profile secret lookup, since a Nodecode
section reads an environment variable, a file, or a secret the settings
sheet files away; and the toolset/check_fn hiding of the tools while no
token is set, because the section itself refuses at start instead.
